# /auto_install.conf for the Deep32 TEST image (BASE lane). Inside the test ramdisk only; a real image has none,
# because d32setup writes the response file at run time with run-time device names (INSTALLER 2.4).
# Keys are a non-ambiguous part of each install.sub question, matched case-insensitively at word boundaries and
# consumed once (_autorespond, OpenBSD 8.0). The placeholders are filled by release/mkimage.sh.
System hostname = deep32
Network interface to configure = done
DNS domain name = test.invalid
Password for root account = @ROOT_HASH@
Public ssh key for root account = none
Start sshd(8) by default = no
Do you expect to run the X Window System = yes
Do you want the X Window System to be started by xenodm(1) = no
Change the default console to com0 = yes
Which speed should com0 use = 115200
Setup a user = d32test
Full name for user d32test = Deep32 Test
Password for user d32test = *************
Public ssh key for user d32test = none
Allow root ssh login = no
What timezone are you in = UTC
Which disk is the root disk = @ROOT_DISK@
Encrypt the root disk with a (p)assphrase or (k)eydisk = no
Use (W)hole disk MBR, whole disk (G)PT = whole
URL to autopartitioning template for disklabel = file:///@TEMPLATE@
Location of sets = disk
Is the disk partition already mounted = no
Which disk contains the install media = @MEDIA_DISK@
partition has the install sets = a
Pathname to the sets = 8.0/amd64
Set name(s) = -comp* -game* +site*
Unverified sets: site80.tgz. Continue without verification = yes
